A small collection of everyday arithmetic helpers for whole numbers and decimals.

Negative exponents quietly return zero, and square roots reject negative input.

Use core.

Publicly, to find the absolute value of x (a whole number), named abs_i64, giving a whole number.
If x is negative, give back 0 minus x.
Give back x.

Publicly, to find the absolute value of x (a decimal), named abs_f64, giving a decimal.
If x equals 0.0, give back 0.0.
If x is less than 0.0, give back 0.0 minus x.
Give back x.

Publicly, to find the smaller of a and b (whole numbers), named min_i64, giving a whole number.
If a is less than b, give back a.
Give back b.

Publicly, to find the larger of a and b (whole numbers), named max_i64, giving a whole number.
If a is more than b, give back a.
Give back b.

Publicly, to find the smaller of a and b (decimals), named min_f64, giving a decimal.
If a is less than b, give back a.
Give back b.

Publicly, to find the larger of a and b (decimals), named max_f64, giving a decimal.
If a is more than b, give back a.
Give back b.

Publicly, to find the square root of x (a decimal), named sqrt, giving a decimal.
If x is less than 0.0, stop with error "sqrt of negative number".
If x equals 0.0, give back 0.0.
Let guess start at 1.0.
If x is at least 1.0, set guess to 0.5 times x.
Let iteration start at 0.
Repeat until iteration is at least 24.
Set guess to 0.5 times (guess plus x divided by guess).
Add 1 to iteration.
End the loop.
Give back guess.

Publicly, to raise base (a whole number) to exponent (a whole number), named pow_i64, giving a whole number.
If exponent is negative, give back 0.
Let result start at 1.
Let factor start at base.
Let power start at exponent.
Repeat while power is positive.
If power modulo 2 is one, multiply result by factor.
Square factor.
Halve power.
End the loop.
Give back result.

Publicly, to clamp value (a whole number) between low (a whole number) and high (a whole number), named clamp_i64, giving a whole number.
If value is less than low, give back low.
If value is more than high, give back high.
Give back value.
